'''Union of Souls''' is a type of [[monster modifier]]. Originally a {{c|bloodline|[[Bloodline modifier|Bloodline]]}} modifier, it has been rework and ported to the [[Archnemesis modifier|new monster modifier pool]] in 3.18 and then the current mod pool in 3.20.0.

All variants of this modifier grants stat {{c|mod|Grants #% increased [[Character Size]] and #% increased Maximum Life to Pack Members on death}} (to remaining monsters for the map mod variant).
==Sources==
* {{il|Valdo Map}} mod {{ml|MapSupporterUnionOfSouls}}
** {{C|mod|Grants #% increased Character Size and #% increased Maximum Life to remaining normal and rarity monsters on death}}
* Monster mod {{ml|MonsterModUnionOfSouls|display=verbose}} (known as {{c|normal|Empowers Allies}} under the monster nameplate)
** Despite it is the same "Empowers Allies" wording as [[Host Chieftain]], [[Power Totem]]'s [[Modifier:MonsterUsesMassPowerText|legacy monster reminder text]], it is does not grants allies {{stl|Power Charge}}

==Version history==
The following are legacy monster mods that related to Union of Souls: 
* {{c|bloodline|Bloodlines}}
**{{ml|MonsterBloodlinesUnionOfSouls|display=verbose}}
* Archnemesis
**{{ml|MonsterArchnemesisUnionOfSouls}}: {{c|mod|Monster's minions are empowered. Minions empower the Monster with additional modifiers on death}} (as "Empowering Minions", Archnemesis league only mod)
***{{ml|MonsterArchnemesisMinionUnionofSouls|display=verbose}}
**{{ml|MonsterArchnemesisUnionOfSoulsMagic|display=verbose}} (as <span style="color:olive">[[Union of Souls]]</span>)
{{Version history table header}}
{{Version history table row|3.20.0|
* Monster mods now only do one specific thing.
* Monster mods now say exactly what they do.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.19.0|
* We have toned down the modifiers that can spawn on magic monsters so that more of them are stat-based bonuses that aren't too spammy. All monsters in an instance that are the same or very similar will have the same magic monster modifier, rather than rolling a different Archnemesis modifier for each monster.
* Some of the more powerful Monster modifiers now use a special reward conversion system. 
}}
{{Version history table row|3.18.0|
* Archnemesis modifiers have been rebalanced and added to the core game. Existing Magic and Rare monster modifiers have been replaced with Archnemesis modifiers.
* Bloodlines and Nemesis have been removed from the core game. Some of their modifiers have been incorporated into the new monster modifier system:
** Union of Souls can be found on Magic monsters.
}}
{{Version history table row|3.17.0|
* Archnemesis monster modifiers are introduced to the game for [[Archnemesis league]]. Some mods incorporated some elements of bloodline modifiers. e.g. "Empowering Minions"
}}
{{Version history table row|2.0.0|
* Bloodlines Mods have been added to the core game.
}}
{{Version history table row|1.3.0|
* Introduced to the game in [[Bloodlines league]].
}}
{{Version history table end}}

